.TH K7CTL 1 "November 2026" "k7ctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
k7ctl \- FiiO K7 status, bit\-perfect setup and headphone EQ for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k7ctl
.RB [ \-\-notify ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B k7ctl
shows what a FiiO K7 DAC/headphone amplifier is receiving (sample rate, bit depth, PCM or DSD)
and sets up PipeWire so it gets the music unchanged: at its own sample rate, without software
volume, and without being suspended when idle. It can also put a headphone EQ (AutoEQ
profiles) in front of the K7, and has a system tray icon and output for status bars.
.PP
The K7 has no volume, gain or input controls over USB: the knob and switches are physical only,
so no software can change them. Sound itself needs no driver; the K7 is a standard USB audio
device.
.PP
Other USB DACs work too: see
.B devices
and
.BR use .
.PP
Without a command,
.B k7ctl
runs
.BR status .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Show the command's result as a desktop notification instead of printing it (for the
launcher actions and keyboard shortcuts). Needs
.BR notify\-send .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Status
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-format " text|json|waybar|short] [" \-\-json "] [" \-w | \-\-watch "] [" \-\-interval " \fIseconds\fR]"
What the K7 is playing, each application playing to it and whether it is being resampled,
firmware, PipeWire volume, allowed sample rates, latency, keep\-awake and EQ. Explains why a
stream is resampled (usually another application that started first at a different rate).
.B waybar
prints Waybar JSON,
.B short
a few characters for other status bars; with
.B \-\-watch
a new line is printed whenever something changes. Exits 1 if no K7 is connected.
.TP
.BR firmware " [" \-\-open ]
The installed firmware version and how to update it. k7ctl does not flash firmware.
.B \-\-open
opens FiiO's firmware download page to compare versions (FiiO has no update API to check
automatically).
.TP
.B diag
A diagnostics report for bug reports: versions, the device's kernel status, PipeWire
settings, k7ctl's files and the EQ service log. The window's "Copy diagnostics" button copies
the same report.
.TP
.BR exclusive " [on|off|status]"
Release the DAC from PipeWire (its profile is set to "off") so a player can open its ALSA device
directly, e.g. MPD for native DSD; other apps play through another output meanwhile.
.B off
restores the previous profile and default output. WirePlumber remembers it, so the DAC stays
released (also after a reboot) until
.BR "exclusive off" .
.SS Device
.TP
.B devices
List USB sound cards with their USB ids; * marks the one k7ctl uses.
.TP
.BI use " vvvv:pppp" \fR|\fBauto
Use another USB DAC (by its USB id from
.BR devices ),
or
.B auto
for the FiiO K7. Keep\-awake and the EQ move to it if they are on. Saved in
.IR ~/.config/k7ctl/settings.json ;
the
.B K7CTL_DEVICE
environment variable overrides it.
.SS Bit\-perfect playback
.TP
.BR rates " [enable|disable|status]"
Let PipeWire switch the K7 to the sample rate of what is playing (44.1 to 384 kHz) instead of
resampling everything to 48 kHz. Applied immediately and saved in
.IR ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/50\-k7ctl\-samplerates.conf .
.TP
.B volume\-max
Set PipeWire's volume for the K7 to 100% and unmute it. Lower software volume reduces
resolution; use the K7's knob instead. Turn the knob down first.
.TP
.BR setup " [" \-y | \-\-yes ]
.BR "rates enable" ,
make the K7 the default output, and
.B volume\-max
(asks first unless
.BR \-\-yes ).
.SS Reliability
.TP
.BR keepawake " [on|off|status] [" \-\-no\-restart ]
Stop WirePlumber suspending the K7 after a few idle seconds, which can cut off the start of
sounds. Saved in
.IR ~/.config/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/50\-k7ctl\-keepawake.conf ;
WirePlumber is restarted to apply it (about a second of silence) unless
.BR \-\-no\-restart .
.TP
.BR latency " [default|stable|low\-latency]"
PipeWire buffer size presets.
.B stable
uses bigger buffers, which fixes crackles at high sample rates;
.B low\-latency
smaller ones for games and calls. Without a preset, shows the current one. Applied immediately
and saved in
.IR ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/51\-k7ctl\-latency.conf .
.SS Headphone EQ
With EQ on, playback is processed and no longer bit\-perfect.
.TP
.BI "eq search " headphone
Search the AutoEQ database of headphone profiles.
.TP
.BI "eq get " headphone \fR\ [\fB\-\-source \fIsource\fR] [\fB\-\-name \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-on\fR]
Download a profile; with several measurements of the same model, pick one with
.BR \-\-source .
.TP
.BI "eq import " file \fR\ [\fB\-\-name \fIname\fR]
Import a parametric EQ in the Equalizer APO format (AutoEQ's ParametricEQ.txt).
.TP
.BR "eq on" " [\fIprofile\fR]"
Turn EQ on: starts the
.B k7ctl\-eq
systemd user service, which adds a "FiiO K7 + EQ" output in front of the K7 and makes it the
default.
.TP
.B eq off
Stop the EQ and make the K7 the default output again.
.TP
.B eq toggle
Turn the EQ on (with the selected profile) or off.
.TP
.BR "eq list" ", " "eq status" ", " "eq remove \fIprofile\fR"
Saved profiles, whether EQ is on, delete a profile.
.SS Desktop
.TP
.B gui
A window with the status, the streams playing to the K7 and all of the above settings,
including searching and downloading EQ profiles, a plot of the selected profile's frequency
response, the DAC to use, and notifications for rate changes and resampling (shown by the
tray icon).
.TP
.B tray
A system tray icon with the status and common settings; click it to open the window. Without a
system tray, opens the window instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/k7ctl/eq/
Saved EQ profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/k7ctl/eq.json
The selected EQ profile.
.TP
.I ~/.config/k7ctl/settings.json
The DAC to use and notification settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/k7ctl\-eq.service
The EQ service, while EQ is on.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/k7ctl\-tray.desktop
Starts the tray icon at login (the tray's "Start at login").
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B K7CTL_DEVICE
A USB id (vvvv:pppp) or
.BR auto ;
overrides the device chosen with
.BR use .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors or when no K7 is connected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
k7ctl setup
k7ctl status \-\-watch
k7ctl eq get "Sennheiser HD 600" \-\-source oratory1990 \-\-on
k7ctl latency stable
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR pw\-metadata (1)
.PP
https://github.com/doodersrage/fiio-k7-linux
